A||||1||JohnnyK||Need help w/ parking light bulb removal?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||02-03-2001||02:09 PM||||Still trying to get that parking light bulb out from under the headlight. I took off the torx screws, but that does nothing. I can sort of pull the whole assembly out an inch or two (thats stretching though, don't want to snap a wire) but I can't get to the bulb.  From the looks of my haynes manual, the orange lense and the black back cover should seperate from the bulb and assembly. NO such luck though? There seems to be some foamish stuff where the bulb assembly and black cover should meet. I tried prying there but to no avail. What shoudl I do? There isn't enough wire slack to get a good look at it. Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||02-03-2001||03:49 PM||||Figured it out. You had to twist it, and it was corroded/stuck. Replaced the bulb and all is good. This would be a lot easier if it wasn't -20 or soemthing outside.||||reg||1
